===Pronunciation===
{{fi-pronunciation}}

===Noun===
{{fi-noun}}

# [[stone]], [[rock]] {{gloss|material}}
## a piece of [[stone]] which is larger than a grain of sand
##: {{syn|fi|musa|qq1=colloquial|mosa|qq2=dialectal|musari|qq3=colloquial, Helsinki}}
##: {{par|fi|kivenmurikka|murikka|q1=large stone/rock}}
## [[rock]] {{gloss|relatively small mass of stone projecting out of the ground}}
##: {{par|fi|kallio}}
## [[boulder]]
##: {{syn|fi|lohkare|kivenlohkare|siirtolohkare}}
## {{n-g|A general term for solid, mineral-based construction materials, such as [[brick]], [[concrete]] or natural stone.}}
# {{lb|fi|nautical|informal}} an underwater [[rock]] which may be dangerous for seafarers
#: {{syn|fi|kari}}
# {{ellipsis of|fi|jalokivi|t=[[rock]], [[jewel]]}}
#: {{uxi|fi|Tässä kellossa on 17 '''kiveä'''.|This clockwork mechanism is made with 17 '''jewels'''.}}
#: {{uxi|fi|Katso tuota '''kiveä''' hänen sormessaan!|Look at that '''rock''' on her finger!}}
# {{lb|fi|colloquial|snooker|pool|billiards}} [[cue ball]]
#: {{syn|fi|lyöntipallo}}
# {{lb|fi|colloquial|computer hardware}} [[central processing unit]]
#: {{syn|fi|suoritin|keskussuoritin|prosessori}}

====Usage notes====
A large mass of stone projecting out of ground is called {{m|fi|kallio}}. Also, if the stone mass is known or assumed to be part of [[bedrock]], it is called {{m|fi|kallio}} even if the visible part is small. Similarly, if a large stone mass is known not to be part of bedrock, it may be called {{m|fi|kivi}} or {{m|fi|lohkare}}.

